    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1724 by the Mughal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-jah-i">Nizam-ul-Mulk</a>, Asaf Jah I, who made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> his hereditary domain.</li><li>A British ally under a subsidiary alliance from 1798, it became the largest and richest princely state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</li><li>Its last Nizam sought independence in 1947; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> annexed the state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-polo">Operation Polo</a> in September 1948.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osmania-university">Osmania University</a>, founded in 1918, taught in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urdu">Urdu</a>, and a state translation bureau rendered textbooks in medicine, engineering and law into the language.</p></aside>
    </section>

